ask 05 — Trunking, 802.1Q and Native VLAN

Objective

To learn VLAN trunking and 802.1Q configuration using Cisco Packet Tracer

Tasks Performed

Created VLAN 10 (HR), VLAN 20 (IT), and VLAN 30 (SALES) on both switches

Assigned access ports to the correct VLANs

Configured trunk ports between two Cisco 2960 switches

Configured Native VLAN 10

Tested communication between PCs in the same VLAN

Configured Allowed VLAN List and blocked VLAN 30 traffic

Created and fixed a Native VLAN mismatch using CDP

Used Simulation Mode to observe packet flow between switches

Verification Commands

show vlan brief
show interfaces trunk
show interfaces status
show cdp neighbors
show logging

Learning Outcomes

Learned VLAN trunking and 802.1Q

Understood Native VLAN

Practiced VLAN filtering

Observed packet flow in Simulation Mode

Learned Native VLAN mismatch troubleshooting


